# sapintegrationsuite_api_provider (Resource)

An API provider describes a backend system that API proxies forward requests to: host, port,
TLS and credentials. Proxies reference it by name instead of carrying the backend details
themselves, so a backend can move without touching every proxy.

**Status:** partial. Backed by `APIProviders` of the API portal's `Management.svc`. SAP's own
tooling supports only creating API providers through the API, so there is no update, and only
the Internet connection type is implemented.

## Prerequisites

- The `api_management` block in the provider configuration, with a key of the API portal
  service plan `apiportal-apiaccess` and the role `APIPortal.Administrator`.
- A backend reachable over the internet.

## Lifecycle

| Operation | What happens |
|---|---|
| Create | Creates the provider, then waits until it is readable; SAP caches reads for about 20 seconds. |
| Read | Reads the connection settings. The password is never read. |
| Update | None. |
| Replacement | Any change deletes the provider and creates it again. Proxies that use it are briefly without a backend. |
| Delete | Deletes the provider. |

The password (`password_wo`) is write-only and sent only when the provider is created; it has no
version attribute, because the provider cannot be updated anyway.

